      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "First, we need to rewrite the equation so that the expression we have is the sum of squares. This is done by completing the square. We write the given equation as:\n\n\\[x^2 - 6x + y^2 + 2y + 6 = 0\\]\n\nCompleting the square for the x and y terms, we have:\n\n\\[(x^2 - 6x) + (y^2 + 2y) + 6 = 0\\]\n\n\\[(x - 3)^2 - 9 + (y + 1)^2 - 1 + 6 = 0\\]\n\n\\[(x - 3)^2 + (y + 1)^2 - 4 = 0\\]\n\n\\[(x - 3)^2 + (y + 1)^2 = 4\\]\n\nThis is the equation of a circle with center (3, -1) and radius \\(\\sqrt{4} = 2\\).\n\nThus, the radius of the circle is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
